{
  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent underprediction in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show a clear uptrend/breakout, add an upward level shift to the whole path (model is ~8–12 EUR too low across much of the horizon in the examples).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the model reacts too slowly to momentum; apply a positive drift correction that increases with horizon (small in week 1, larger by weeks 2–4) when recent slope is positive.",
    "Volatility compression: the model forecast range is too narrow versus realized moves; widen the forecast fan and lift peaks during rallies (do not cap prices near the recent mean when momentum is strong).",
    "Mean-reversion bias in bull runs: the model pulls back toward ~70–73 even as the market trends to 80+; reduce mean-reversion strength when price is making higher highs (e.g., above recent 20–30d high).",
    "Horizon-specific bias: errors grow with lead time; apply an increasing additive correction by horizon (e.g., +3–5 EUR days 1–7, +6–9 EUR days 8–20, +8–12 EUR days 21–30) when regime is bullish."
  ]
}
